# Refactoring & Upgrade Rules for Business Central AL

1. [cite_start]PRESERVE BUSINESS LOGIC: Do not rewrite core posting algorithms in active Codeunits (e.g., 85001, 85002, 85025, 85040)[cite: 539, 540, 543, 549]. [cite_start]Only re-bind record variables and delegate page writes[cite: 550].
2. [cite_start]ZERO CROSS-DOMAIN DIRECT WRITES: Codeunits in domain X must never execute direct Insert/Modify/Delete on tables in domain Y. Use Integration Events or Service Codeunits instead.
3. [cite_start]EXTEND NATIVE BC TABLES: Prefer extending standard tables (Customer, Resource, Item, Vendor) via Table Extensions over creating duplicate custom master entities[cite: 510, 551].
4. [cite_start]INCREMENTAL COMPILATION: Run AL compilation (`Ctrl+Shift+B` or `AL: Package`) after refactoring every module[cite: 586]. [cite_start]Fix all compilation errors before moving to the next prompt[cite: 572, 586].